  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-1",
      "transcript": "Why can a hotter pan make a drop of water last longer?",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 3.85,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.f99c6b30c5958c094afecafa33745022a329429e69697c85b7e7dcc2777c79be",
        "sha256": "f99c6b30c5958c094afecafa33745022a329429e69697c85b7e7dcc2777c79be"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-2",
      "transcript": "On a hot metal surface, water can touch the metal and boil away quickly.",
      "start": 4.433333333333334,
      "duration": 4.95,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.963302dd75ba0e05944aa4770e2759d64710dc9b11c1c9ae1cae9f34924eaeaf",
        "sha256": "963302dd75ba0e05944aa4770e2759d64710dc9b11c1c9ae1cae9f34924eaeaf"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-3",
      "transcript": "Heat it far enough, and something changes.",
      "start": 9.666666666666666,
      "duration": 2.875,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.1fa56bad97b6d02f3bc81a7ad6b1e475e2e2ae7d966df63cf0162159b41aac1a",
        "sha256": "1fa56bad97b6d02f3bc81a7ad6b1e475e2e2ae7d966df63cf0162159b41aac1a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-4",
      "transcript": "The bottom of the drop turns to vapor almost instantly.",
      "start": 12.833333333333334,
      "duration": 3.825,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.35845b13cd856696a67d0b4044014e8b5f10b684f2ffdc7b5869115a42f2ccef",
        "sha256": "35845b13cd856696a67d0b4044014e8b5f10b684f2ffdc7b5869115a42f2ccef"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-5",
      "transcript": "That vapor forms a cushion, lifting the rest of the water off the metal.",
      "start": 16.933333333333334,
      "duration": 4.525,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.01e17275abb3597e5b0bd5504d643696e75c3ebb704054eb38f55c023e88ca1a",
        "sha256": "01e17275abb3597e5b0bd5504d643696e75c3ebb704054eb38f55c023e88ca1a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Now heat must cross a poorly conducting gas layer.",
      "start": 22.033333333333335,
      "duration": 3.625,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.8d2eeb31f5a1b8d19b763a0c66e76a2792b7546d448c5cb51bb530136ec2a6f6",
        "sha256": "8d2eeb31f5a1b8d19b763a0c66e76a2792b7546d448c5cb51bb530136ec2a6f6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-7",
      "transcript": "The hotter surface has created a barrier to its own heat.",
      "start": 25.933333333333334,
      "duration": 3.775,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.35205d7722a2596b24bbe87136996056c3b572d11b9ee09fff0cc0834a9e7a80",
        "sha256": "35205d7722a2596b24bbe87136996056c3b572d11b9ee09fff0cc0834a9e7a80"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-8",
      "transcript": "This is the Leidenfrost effect.",
      "start": 30.3,
      "duration": 2.625,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.81af62fc12c86813eb7a64b204939e9a32fc889033032600aa4103ff2e9f0e2f",
        "sha256": "81af62fc12c86813eb7a64b204939e9a32fc889033032600aa4103ff2e9f0e2f"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-9",
      "transcript": "It doesn’t mean hotter always makes water last longer.",
      "start": 33.2,
      "duration": 3.525,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.c9d57e3ac3b2b1ab55c6a8fe7854bde9b230a52a060021d3c81b30334afa3f6a",
        "sha256": "c9d57e3ac3b2b1ab55c6a8fe7854bde9b230a52a060021d3c81b30334afa3f6a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-10",
      "transcript": "The transition depends on the surface and the drop.",
      "start": 37,
      "duration": 3.675,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.c85742f1068199d2192650b4a0df0d0478980700e6320e96b194c5b321fb59d5",
        "sha256": "c85742f1068199d2192650b4a0df0d0478980700e6320e96b194c5b321fb59d5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-11",
      "transcript": "Above it, more heat can speed evaporation again.",
      "start": 40.96666666666667,
      "duration": 3.525,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.cf3f15eb071deda98cd95f333a62bcf1e3c23fc2b8fbfea0da405a200b95032b",
        "sha256": "cf3f15eb071deda98cd95f333a62bcf1e3c23fc2b8fbfea0da405a200b95032b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heat-cue-12",
      "transcript": "The surprise is that a hotter surface can give water less direct contact with the heat.",
      "start": 44.766666666666666,
      "duration": 5.6,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.0f3751b42f9ee1fd130f915624badc27df9bb8128552238ed05883d55d4c2da2",
        "sha256": "0f3751b42f9ee1fd130f915624badc27df9bb8128552238ed05883d55d4c2da2"
      }
    }
  ],
